 "final_summary": "The issue was that non-positive values from environment variables were being directly used without falling back to the default. The fix in `tracker/config.py` modifies the `_coerce` function to return the default value when a non-positive integer is parsed, ensuring proper fallback behavior. This resolves the test failure and maintains the intended configuration precedence.",
